Portal modifications (2026):
- Detector.js returns measured finder-square outlines instead of inventing a
  fourth corner for QR version 1; it exposes geometry to the pose solver.
- FinderPatternFinder.js scans all rows rather than terminating at the first
  apparently confirmed triple; this avoids a tested false-positive triple.
  It also accepts foreshortened finder widths and selects supported non-degenerate
  triples without the mean-module-width filter. Detector.js checks alternative
  corner assignments and nearby dimensions against decoded payloads.
- geometry.js fits a projective transform to the measured outlines and estimates
  and refines a rigid pose, with bounded focal estimation when an uncalibrated
  guess fails. core-entry.js samples and decodes the rectified grid.
- Detector.js also exposes a finder-centre-only acquisition pass. core-entry.js
  provides decoded references; Portal-owned tracking.js adds sparse optical flow,
  bounded confidence checks and sparse appearance validation without QR decoding.
  The Portal adapter manages native video ROIs and adaptive verification timing.
- centre-tracking.js follows inner black islands using local optical flow and
  darkness-weighted centres, with shape and shared-motion checks. The worker
  runs the same engine with transferred frames and bounded scheduling.
- No browser reader, camera acquisition, or MediaStream lifecycle is bundled.

Also includes ts-custom-error, MIT license; see LICENSE-ts-custom-error.
The generated core.js contains the pinned dependencies and the Portal changes.
